WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back.
-Thank you very much.

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.671
Thank you for having me again.
-We're so, so happy to have you

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
back in New York City.
-Yeah.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.041 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So thrilled.

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:10.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's very nice of you.
Thank you very much.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you -- This is nice
to have you here.

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:13.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're obviously working.
That's why you're in New York.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you get to do Thanksgiving
in New York.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:16.049 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes. Yeah, yeah.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:17.650
My girlfriend and I are hosting
for the first time.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is that something you've done
before? No, first time.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:20.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I've never done that
before.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah, I thought
I'm just gonna make myself --

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:25.091 size:84% position:42% line:92%
you know, I can't cook.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:27.293
So I'm gonna just make myself
as useful as humanly possible.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.929
I thought I was gonna be doing
some maybe chopping of things.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:33.633
I found out yesterday I'm not
gonna be trusted with chopping.

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:34.100 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wow.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:34.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's probably
a good decision.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
-'Cause chopping is
the lowest as far as --

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no, no.
Stirring is the lowest.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:41.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Stirring is -- You're right.
Stirring is lower.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.042 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Stirring is lower.

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:44.377
-So are they gonna have you
doing a little stirring?

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.145 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I'm gonna be stirring.

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:46.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna be maybe
crushing things.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's good.
-If that's required, yeah.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:51.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And how many people
are you hosting?

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:52.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Nine.
-Okay.

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:55.388
-Some families will laugh at
that paltry amount of people.

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.856 line:92%
But for me, that's more people

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
then I've, you know,
had in one group.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:02.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
Outside of this kind of room
in a long time.

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:02.929 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Turkey though?

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:03.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yup.
-Okay.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Turkey and then
a bunch of sides.

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:06.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, yes, we've got
a vegetarian.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:08.802 size:81% position:41%
So we sorted them out.
They've got an option.

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:11.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've got a friend
who's allergic to nuts.

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:11.638 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They're sorted.

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:13.673
So, yeah, I've really just --
it's been a week of finding out

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:15.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
everybody's dietary
restrictions.

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:16.176 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:17.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that is the new problem
in this day and age.

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.345
-Yes.
-Raises the level of difficulty.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Will you watch --
we've talked before.

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:22.115 line:92%
-Football. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:24.651
-You became a football fan,
an American football fan.

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:25.385 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Will you be watching?

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:26.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely, yeah.
-Okay.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.755
-That's -- that will be the,
sort of, soundtrack of the day.

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:29.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my girlfriend's
from Michigan.

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:33.093
So we'll be -- there's always
a Lions game on Thanksgiving.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:33.626 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, that's good.

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:34.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
-With the misery or joy
that that entails.

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:37.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, more often than not,
misery, yeah.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It has been.
-Yeah.

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:40.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But, you know, it's -- I feel
like there's a certain --

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:43.036 size:78% position:39%
heartbreak is part of
being a Giants fan.

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:43.536 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, okay.

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:44.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In a way that is
sort of about a lot --

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:47.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, being an English
football fan is also --

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:48.274 size:81% position:41% line:92%
sort of in some way --

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.009 size:78% position:39%
well, growing up was,
you know, mixed in

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:52.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a lot of heartbreak
and missed penalties.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:53.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:55.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And was the World Cup
exciting for you?

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know in the end
it ended in tears.

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:59.652
-No, but that's the furthest
they've gone in my lifetime.

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was amazing.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:02.188 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Don't laugh at that.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:04.757
Just 'cause you're America
and you win stuff all the time.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:05.291 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:08.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember the first time I --
We were in Germany.

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:11.865
The date that everyone in
England grows up knowing is 1966

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the year England
won the World Cup.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's engrained
in all of us.

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:18.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I remember the first time
I went to Germany

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:19.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
and realized no one
there has any idea

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:21.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's what happened that year
or in any other country.

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:24.444
It's not famous. It's just that
we really hang on to that.

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:26.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Oh, no,
you've won it so many times,

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
you don't hang on
to the one year

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:29.215 line:92%
that you won it 50 years ago."

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. But it gets sadder with
every year that passes

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:34.053
'cause the thing that you're
proud of gets a year older.

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:34.854 line:92%
-Further and further away, yeah.

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:37.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I was in Germany this year
for the World Cup,

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:38.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was great,
'cause, you know,

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
they got knocked out
kind of early

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:41.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we did really well.
-There you go.

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:42.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For once.
-There you go.

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's something
to hang your hat on.

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:48.535
So, this show, this is a play
where you play a fact checker.

00:02:48.535 --> 00:02:48.968 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you're dealing with
a reporter who maybe

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:54.174
doesn't have the same love of
facts that your character does.

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:58.411
-I should say he's not so much
a reporter as he's an author.

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.812 line:92%
He's written, kind of, an essay.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he deals in,
sort of -- it's --

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:03.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
it is about fact checking,
but it's --

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.051 line:92%
the thing that you can't --

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:06.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're not a particularly
political play

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:09.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you can't say the word
"fact" at the moment

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:11.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
without it kind of becoming
a political statement.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is --
and that is obviously --

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:14.661 line:92%
we're very topical in that way.

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:17.897
But we're not dealing with Trump
and that stuff and fake news.

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:19.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
We don't, kind of,
get into all that.

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:22.468
But it's more about, kind of,
a debate about artistic license

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.504 size:88% position:44%
and how far you can push
something as a writer.

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:27.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it -- all that other stuff
is encompassed as well.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's 85 minutes long
and really funny.

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah, that's me selling it
to you.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:33.379 size:84% position:42%
-That's a good sell.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:34.414 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You went --

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:37.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
You actually went and worked
a job as a fact checker

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
at "New Yorker" --
at "The New Yorker."

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:40.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, they let me --
they very, very kindly --

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:43.823
"The New Yorker" invited me
to spend a day with their --

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:46.426
or a few hours with their
fact-checking department.

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:48.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they were --
who were all amazing

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:51.965
and just these super bright,
young people who, you know,

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:53.233 line:92%
I'm very grateful for existing.

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.568
And we -- yeah, and they --
I didn't really take it in

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:56.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
when they said
"Oh, you're gonna come

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we'll make you
fact-check an article."

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:01.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Okay, cool.
Yeah, I'll come and see stuff.

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:01.641 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What's going on?"

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:02.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I went
and they were like,

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:04.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
"No, you're gonna get on
the phone to somebody

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:06.546 size:88% position:44%
and actually fact-check
this restaurant review."

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:07.313 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And I suddenly -- I did.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got way more nervous about
that than I do

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
about doing the play
every night or anything.

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:14.320 size:78% position:39%
Just because suddenly
you're on the phone

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.188 line:92%
with somebody who expects --

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:18.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
He knows he's getting a call
from "The New Yorker."

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:19.459 line:92%
He doesn't know it's an actor

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:21.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
playing around
at being a fact checker.

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:22.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:24.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's expecting
a level of professionalism

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:26.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I didn't know
if I had in me. So, yeah.

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:28.401 size:81% position:41%
-How do you fact-check
a restaurant review?

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:31.070 size:84% position:42%
Do you call up and say,
"Was the soup cold?"

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:31.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You do?

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You literally --
you track every --

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:35.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's when I started
underlining the article,

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:37.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is what you do when you
start checking something,

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:39.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
and underline everything
you think is a fact.

00:04:39.746 --> 00:04:42.982
I was like, "Oh, every -- every
ingredient counts as a fact."

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:44.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I guess
I got to ask him about,

00:04:44.651 --> 00:04:45.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Do you put
all these things in?"

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:51.524
And it was -- you know, my --
my big moment was finding out

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:54.494
that something was not, in fact,
seasoned with Old Bay.

00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:56.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was seasoned with
adobe and chili.

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:57.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow!
-Yeah.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that was -- that was --
and but, you know --

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:01.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
you don't know how much
satisfaction I got from then

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:05.772
seeing that restaurant review
with the correct information.

00:05:05.772 --> 00:05:06.205 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:08.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Knowing that I had been
a part of that.

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:08.708 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That is thri--

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:11.511
I mean, that's a fact checker's
dream is to catch one.

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:12.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, God.
-Yeah.

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:14.314
I mean, I would have gotten off
the phone.

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:16.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
And even though
it doesn't make sense,

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:18.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would have screamed,
"Stop the presses."

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:20.653 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:24.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Quickly!
We can't run it like this!

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:27.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah, no -- and it was --
it's really like --

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:28.161 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't know.

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:29.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was something really
inspirational about going into

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:31.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The New Yorker"
and seeing how it's all done.

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:33.499
And also, I did almost feel like
saying at the end,

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:36.436
"You know, if you've ever got
any really low-stakes articles

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:38.571 size:84% position:42%
that you need checking,
I'm happy to do that."

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:41.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
The guy I had to call
was a very, very nice chef

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:42.075 line:92%
who made my job very easy.

00:05:42.075 --> 00:05:44.911
I wouldn't like to be doing that
job if I did have to call,

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:46.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, Sarah Sanders
or somebody

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:48.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
who does not want
to hear from you.

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:49.115 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, that's true.

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:51.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
She might not want to hear
from anybody, though.

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:52.352 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.786 size:88% position:44%
There are certain people
that just don't like it

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:55.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
when the phone rings.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:56.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That's fair enough.

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:57.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And a wonderful cast,
obviously.

00:05:57.924 --> 00:05:59.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
Cherry Jones
and Bobby Cannavale,

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:01.728 line:92%
which all should be noted.

